<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.1.1: Understanding a Situation with Quadratic Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02086</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.1.1: Understanding a Situation with Quadratic Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>cadf6774-1650-427d-b6be-927e7ca2d615</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para>A mechanical device is used to launch a potato vertically into the air. The potato is launched from a platform 20 feet above the ground, with an initial vertical velocity of 92 feet per second.</para>
      <para>The function \(h(t) = -16t^2 + 92t + 20\) models the height of the potato over the ground, in feet, \(t\) seconds after launch.</para>
      <para>Here is the graph representing the function.</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_09_03_02_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <para>For each question, explain your reasoning.</para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the height of the potato 1 second after launch? </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter the height of the potato 1 second after launch.</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The height of the potato 1 second after launch will be 96 feet.
      Substituting 1 second into the function \(h(t)\) yields:</para>
          <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}h(1)&amp;=&amp;-16{(1)}^2+92(1)+2\\&amp;=&amp;-16+92+20\\&amp;=&amp;96\end{array}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Will the potato still be in the air 8 seconds after launch? </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your explanation.</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>No, from the graph, we can see the potato will land before 8 seconds after the launch. </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Will the potato reach 120 feet? If so, when will it happen? </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your explanation.</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Yes, from the graph, we can see the potato’s height will be 120 feet at two times: approximately 1.5 seconds and 4.3 seconds after launch.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>When will the potato hit the ground, or have a height of zero feet? </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Enter your explanation.</para>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para> We can see from the graph the potato will hit the ground, or have a height of zero feet, after approximately 6 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
